From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sinful1992 <sinful1992@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 00:45:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Read a page's media streams in one query instead of one per
 item

MediaSources, MediaStreams, Trickplay and HasLyrics all end in
item.GetMediaStreams(), one database round-trip per item, buried in
Video.GetMediaSources where a batch cannot be threaded through. On this
server that is ~2 ms per item: 276 ms of a 590 ms full-series episode
list, and the same again on a 100-movie grid.

MediaStreamRepository gains GetMediaStreamsByItems (one query, grouped).
MediaSourceManager gains a request-scoped prefetch: an AsyncLocal batch
that GetMediaStreams(query) answers whole-item reads from while the scope
is open, so nothing is cached across requests and there is no staleness
window. DtoService opens the scope for a page whenever a field will read
streams, and only for two or more items.

Neither addition touches MediaBrowser.Controller, the assembly plugins
bind against: the new members sit on the concrete classes and an
internal contract in this assembly, reached by type test.
